s any path outside `.ard/<issue#>/`, the merger merges only when every review passed and required checks are green on the current head (checked in code, not left to GitHub), and the bot-commit audit flags any bot commit on `main` that touches anything else. GitHub enforces nothing on the App's merges, so the merger reads the required checks itself from the branch rules API. A squash merge has GitHub (`noreply@github.com`) as committer and the App as author, so the audit, which keys on the committer, does not cover merges: the merger's gates do.\n\n## Configuration\n\nConfiguration is by convention: a role exists because its directory exists, and `.ard/config.yaml` holds only global settings and overrides. No prompt path is written anywhere; ard reads `.ard/<type>/<name>/prompt.txt`. Model credentials are host settings (`ARD_AGENT_AUTH`, `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN` in the `ard serve` environment), not `config.yaml` keys, because a PR can change `config.yaml`.\nagent: claude                # default CLI for agent roles\nrequire_approval: true       # human adds ard:approved before a worker starts\nbudget_usd_per_day: 50       # whole repo, UTC day, blocks at spent >= cap; a role may set its own; provisional, recalibrated between Gate 1 and Gate 2\nmax_budget_usd: 5            # per job; provisional, same recalibration\nglobal_max_open: 30          # open scanner issues across all scanners\npaused: false\nintervals: { scanners: 4h, triage: 15m, workers: 5m, reviewers: 5m, merger: 5m }\nintake: { mode: label }     # mode: all | label; label (label mode only) defaults to ard:pending, must start with ard: and must not be one of ard's own labels\nmerge:                       # defaults written by `ard init`; the list is the only source (no floor in code)\n  protected_paths: [.github/, .ard/config.yaml, .ard/scanners/, .ard/triage/, .ard/workers/, .ard/reviewers/, \"**/CODEOWNERS\", CLAUDE.md, \"**/CLAUDE.md\", AGENTS.md, \"**/AGENTS.md\", .claude/, .mcp.json, \"**/.golangci.yml\", \"**/.golangci.yaml\", \"**/.golangci.toml\", \"**/.golangci.json\"]\nstale: { inactive_for: 30d, suppress_for: 90d }\n\nsidecars:\n  vpe-specs: { repo: <owner>/specs, ref: main }   # ref: branch, tag or full 40-hex SHA; default main\n\noverrides:                   # only what differs from convention\n  scanners/cve:             { every: 6h, max_open: 10, group_size: 1, autoclose: true }\n  scanners/docs:            { every: 3d, max_open: 3, group_size: 10, autoclose: true }\n  scanners/error-codes:     { every: 24h, group_size: 20, autoclose: true }\n  scanners/missing-tests:   { every: 24h, max_open: 5, group_size: 10, autoclose: true }\n  scanners/trufflehog:      { every: 24h, max_open: 5, group_size: 1, autoclose: true, route: needs-human, timeout: 30m }\n  scanners/lint:            { every: 24h, max_open: 3, group_size: 20, autoclose: true }\n  triage/lead:              { sidecar: vpe-specs, timeout: 15m, model: claude-opus-5-5 }\n  triage/architect:         { sidecar: vpe-specs }\n  triage/engineer:          { after: [architect, product-manager, designer, documentation-planner] }\n  workers/engineer:         { tests: make test, timeout: 60m, reviewers: [security-review, eng-review] }","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Tw576g4T3x5oS6MTt7xrUL","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChMkRYRgkfLpY1vpU8iQB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01P8hwpaA1pX5vfipmMhhjuM","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\ndef sub(p,a,b):\n    s=open(p).read(); assert a in s,a; open(p,'w').write(s.replace(a,b,1))\nP='docs/proposal.md'\nsub(P,'| `ard:needs-human` | Controller, from the agent\\'s result, or a scanner at filing (`route: needs-human`) | Agent reported it is blocked; automation stops |','| `ard:needs-human` | Controller, from the agent\\'s result, a scanner at filing (`route: needs-human`), the merger, or the PR watch loop (a PR closed without merging while its issue is open) | Agent reported it is blocked, or the PR is gone; automation stops |')\nsub(P,'## Configuration\\n\\nConfiguration is by convention','''## PR watch loop\n\nA PR can change state behind ard's back, or stop moving, and the merger sees only ready, open PRs. `internal/prwatch` is a controller loop, not an agent, and takes no slot. Every `intervals.prwatch` (default 5m) it reads ard's PRs (App-authored `worker/` branches with base `main`: draft, ready, merged and closed) and **only observes, records and notifies**. It never merges, updates a branch, re-requests a review or starts a round: those belong to the merger, to #252 (stale reviews), #255 (conflicts) and `reviewfix` (#41), and the loop's effects interface has no such call. It is skipped while the controller is paused, like the merger.\n\n| Change | Action |\n|---|---|\n| A human closes the PR without merging while its issue is open | `ard:needs-human` on the issue and one comment on how to retry (remove `ard:worker:<role>:done`) or close it. Once per PR. Nothing if the issue is closed, a merge is recorded, or another PR of the issue is open |\n| Required checks pending on one head longer than `pr_watch.pending_timeout` (default 2h) | One status-issue notice per (PR, head) naming the pending checks. No label. A new head restarts the clock. The merger's `waiting_checks` gets this answer instead of only a log line (#256) |\n| A human merges the PR | A `merge` event whose data has `pr`, `head` and `actor` (the human), for the digest and the gate counts. Logged, no comment. A merge by the App is not recorded again: the merger already wrote its event |\n| A draft PR's required checks go red | One PR comment per head naming the failed checks. No label. Ready PRs with red checks are the merger's |\n| Head moved, conflicts, requested changes, comments, label edits | Logged only |\n\nChecks are judged by `prgate.EvalChecks`, the same function the merger uses, so the two cannot read one set of checks differently. The loop acts only on PRs it has seen open: it keeps a row per PR in the `pr_watch` table of `_controller.db` (head, checks state, when the head was first seen, and what was notified), so installing it does not replay history. Per tick it makes one `ListPRs(state=all, base=main)` call and reads `RequiredChecks` once, and check runs and commit statuses only for open PRs whose head is not settled; a green or red result is kept per head, so an unchanged head costs no check calls (at most 1+2N calls). A PR with a running worker or review job is skipped. Each action runs at most once per (PR, head, transition): the loop checks the row, a `pr_watch` event `{pr, head, transition}` and a marker comment (`<!-- ard:prwatch <transition> pr=<n> head=<sha> -->`) before it acts, and writes the event and row after the effect, so a restart or a failed write posts nothing twice. Check names come from CI and are untrusted: they are sanitized and printed in code spans, and no PR or issue body text or `@` is ever copied. In `--dry-run` the loop keeps its state in memory, appends no events and writes only to the effects ledger. `ard serve --loops` can leave it out.\n\n## Configuration\n\nConfiguration is by convention''')\nsub(P,'intervals: { scanners: 4h, triage: 15m, workers: 5m, reviewers: 5m, merger: 5m }\\n','intervals: { scanners: 4h, triage: 15m, workers: 5m, reviewers: 5m, merger: 5m, prwatch: 5m }\\npr_watch: { pending_timeout: 2h }   # at least intervals.prwatch, at most 7d\\n')\nsub(P,'It squash-merges with the PR title','Checks that stay pending are reported by the PR watch loop (below), not here. It squash-merges with the PR title')\nL='docs/layout.md'\nsub(L,'internal/prgate/            reviews-passed-at-head decision shared by the reviewer\\'s mark-ready and the merger: label rule, head Covers, reviewed heads, ParseWorkerBranch','internal/prgate/            decisions shared by the reviewer, the merger and prwatch: reviews-passed-at-head (label rule, head Covers, reviewed heads), ParseWorkerBranch, and the check rule (EvalChecks, ResolveApps)')\nsub(L,'internal/reviewfix/','internal/prwatch/           the PR watch loop (#267): observes ard\\'s PRs for closed-unmerged, long-pending checks, human merges and red drafts; labels, comments and events only, never merges; no slot\\ninternal/reviewfix/')\nEOF\ngrep -n \"5m, merger\\|merger: 5m\\|prwatch\" docs/proposal.md | head; grep -rn \"merger: *5m\\|intervals:\" --include=*.md --include=*.yaml . 2>/dev/null | grep -v proposal | head"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5346,"cache_read_input_tokens":130414,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5346},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"38b45f0e-1977-46fe-92b9-68df068f9fb5","uuid":"110091f9-9e6f-4dd2-9b64-cad49bb2ad14","timestamp":"2026-11-24T12:25:51.964Z","request_id":"req_011ChMkRY56QTRnawKWFJkzm"}
